ef text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling .", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le11ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past tense and Past Continuous tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished.<br>You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.<br><span class=\"bullet\"> Regular verbs end in -ed or -ied.</span><br><span class=\"bullet\"> Irregular verbs change in different ways.</span><br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary  <span class=\"italic\">did </span>followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask ... ?</span><br> <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>.<br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For Past Continuous, we add  <span class=\"italic\">was/were + verb\u201cing\u201d</span> to verbs.  Some verbs need a drop to the last letter to add \u201cing\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" talk\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" talked  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were talking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" walk   \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"walked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were walking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"t